{"title":"Career Roadmap · Museum Assistant","role":"Museum Assistant","summary":"A Museum Assistant supports the day-to-day management, documentation, preservation, interpretation and public presentation of museum collections. With an Anthropology background, the strongest opportunities are in anthropology, archaeology, ethnography, cultural heritage and human-history collections.","facts":{},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A B.Sc in Anthropology provides a useful foundation, but progression into specialist museum, curatorial, conservation or research positions often benefits from a relevant PG qualification and museum/heritage experience."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career Stage","Typical Direction"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"Foundation + exposure"},{"text":"Museum Intern / Collection Assistant"}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"Early professional"},{"text":"Museum Assistant / Collections Assistant"}],[{"text":"2035–2040"},{"text":"Specialist"},{"text":"Museum Educator / Collections Specialist / Assistant Curator"}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"Senior"},{"text":"Curator / Museum Programme Manager / Heritage Specialist"}]]}]},{"heading":"What to Build During B.Sc","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Year","Main Focus","Skills to Build","Proof of Progress"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1"},{"text":"Anthropology foundation"},{"text":"Human evolution, archaeology, cultural anthropology, social anthropology"},{"text":"Collection/documentation project"}],[{"text":"Year 2"},{"text":"Museum & heritage knowledge"},{"text":"Material culture, ethnography, heritage, archival basics"},{"text":"Museum observation report"}],[{"text":"Year 3"},{"text":"Collection management"},{"text":"Cataloguing, object handling, documentation, research"},{"text":"Museum/heritage internship"}],[{"text":"Year 4"},{"text":"P